{"id": "en_story_gimli", "tag": "AVIATION", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#FF9F43", "lang": "en", "total": 68.85, "segments": [{"text": "On 23 July 1983 an Air Canada Boeing 767 runs out of fuel at high altitude.", "start": 0.0, "end": 5.42}, {"text": "Ground crews calculate fuel in pounds instead of kilograms during the busy flight from Montreal.", "start": 5.88, "end": 9.78}, {"text": "Only about 10,100 kg of fuel sits on board instead of the 22,300 kg needed.", "start": 10.3, "end": 15.76}, {"text": "Both massive engines suddenly stop running at about 41,000 feet in the freezing sky.", "start": 16.3, "end": 20.38}, {"text": "All glass cockpit screens go dark while emergency power comes from a small spinning turbine.", "start": 20.94, "end": 24.94}, {"text": "Winnipeg sits too far away to reach safely with the dead jet engines.", "start": 25.56, "end": 28.18}, {"text": "First officer Maurice Quintal remembers an old air force base located right at Gimli.", "start": 28.18, "end": 32.24}, {"text": "The abandoned runway is actively hosting a car race with campers parked nearby.", "start": 32.6, "end": 36.14}, {"text": "Captain Bob Pearson uses his personal glider pilot experience to control the silent aircraft.", "start": 36.88, "end": 40.68}, {"text": "The skilled pilot executes a rare forward slip maneuver to rapidly lose dangerous altitude.", "start": 41.18, "end": 45.06}, {"text": "The nose landing gear collapses completely as the heavy metal jet scrapes the tarmac.", "start": 45.52, "end": 49.04}, {"text": "Sparks fly everywhere as the sliding passenger airplane finally comes to a complete stop.", "start": 49.5, "end": 53.28}, {"text": "Remarkably all 69 people on board survive this terrifying emergency with only minor injuries.", "start": 53.94, "end": 58.34}, {"text": "Maintenance crews repair the damaged jet and it continues flying safely until 2008.", "start": 58.88, "end": 62.42}, {